{
  "id": "duration-aida",
  "title": "Duration : 間",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "content": "**間** expresses a span of time : how long something lasted or how long an action continued. It attaches directly after the duration amount."
    },
    {
      "type": "pattern",
      "lines": [
        "[Duration] + **間** + [action / state]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "vocab_table",
      "columns": [
        "japanese",
        "romaji",
        "english"
      ],
      "rows": [
        {
          "japanese": "三時間",
          "romaji": "sanjikan",
          "english": "for three hours"
        },
        {
          "japanese": "一週間",
          "romaji": "isshūkan",
          "english": "for one week"
        },
        {
          "japanese": "二年間",
          "romaji": "ninenkan",
          "english": "for two years"
        },
        {
          "japanese": "十分間",
          "romaji": "juppunkan",
          "english": "for ten minutes"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "example_table",
      "columns": [
        "japanese",
        "romaji",
        "english"
      ],
      "rows": [
        {
          "japanese": "三時間勉強しました。",
          "romaji": "Sanjikan benkyō shimashita.",
          "english": "I studied for three hours."
        },
        {
          "japanese": "一週間日本にいました。",
          "romaji": "Isshūkan nihon ni imashita.",
          "english": "I was in Japan for one week."
        },
        {
          "japanese": "二年間日本語を学んでいます。",
          "romaji": "Ninenkan nihongo wo manande imasu.",
          "english": "I have been learning Japanese for two years."
        },
        {
          "japanese": "十分間待ちました。",
          "romaji": "Juppunkan machimashita.",
          "english": "I waited for ten minutes."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "content": "間 has two readings. Combined with numbers it reads **かん** (三時間, 一週間). Used alone or in short phrases it can read **あいだ** (この間 = recently, the other day). In duration expressions, かん is almost always correct."
    }
  ]
}